Command-line client for A2A agents, built on a2a-protocol-client.

Every command prints its result to stdout as JSON. Exit codes: 0 success, 1 protocol or transport error (message on stderr, plus the agent's JSON error object when there is one), 2 usage error.

Usage: a2a [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  card    Fetch the agent card and print it; or sign or verify a card
  audit   Verify an exported audit chain (offline)
  send    Send one text message (`SendMessage`) and print the task or message
  stream  Send one text message and stream the events (`SendStreamingMessage`), one JSON object per line, until the terminal event
  task    Inspect, cancel or list tasks
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --binding <BINDING>
          Protocol binding to speak to <URL> with. Without this flag the agent card is fetched from <URL>/.well-known/agent-card.json and the binding is chosen the way ClientBuilder::from_card does: the first interface the card lists that this client supports (spec §8.3.2) — and the card's URL for that interface is used, not <URL>. With this flag no card is fetched and <URL> is taken as the endpoint of that binding 
